

From: Kyrylo Tkachov <ktkachov@nvidia.com>

The switch-dispatch transformation trades code size for dispatch speed.  At
-O2 on an AArch64 Olympus system it improves mawk by 5.7% and QuickJS-ng by
25.2%.  Their text changes are 3.73% and 0.90%, respectively.  At -Ofast it
improves 714.cpython_r by 7.7% with a 0.20% text change.

Enable the option at -O2 for speed builds, where the existing computed-goto
unfactoring also runs.  Keep it disabled for -Os, -Oz, and size-optimized
functions.  It applies to every target that does not refuse to share jump
tables through TARGET_CAN_SHARE_JUMP_TABLE_P.

Jeff Law approved v3 of this patch (4/7), provided that the patches it
depends on are approved:
https://inbox.sourceware.org/gcc-patches/6beb9fd7-5e52-49d1-988e-1ed36582d1ea@oss.qualcomm.com/

gcc/ChangeLog:

	PR middle-end/126236
	* opts.cc (default_options_table): Enable
	-fduplicate-switch-dispatch at -O2 for speed builds.
	* doc/invoke.texi: Document it.  List it among the options that
	-Os does not enable.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	PR middle-end/126236
	* gcc.dg/switch-dispatch-5.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/switch-dispatch-1.c: Test default enablement at
	-O2.

Signed-off-by: Kyrylo Tkachov <ktkachov@nvidia.com>
---
Changes since v3:
- In v3, this patch changed code only on AArch64.  With 3/8 and 4/8,
  the same opts.cc entry changes code on every target that does not opt
  out through TARGET_CAN_SHARE_JUMP_TABLE_P, such as x86_64 and RISC-V.
- The patch moves from 4/7 to 8/8, after the port opt-outs (4/8), the
  verifier (6/8) and the RISC-V vsetvl fix (7/8).  Without 7/8, the
  option can cause an ICE in rtl_split_edge on RISC-V vector code.
- A new test, gcc.dg/switch-dispatch-5.c, checks the -O2 default.  It
  runs on all targets.  On shared_jump_tables targets, it also checks
  that the compgotos dump shows two shared tables.
- doc/invoke.texi now lists -fduplicate-switch-dispatch among the -O2
  options that -Os does not enable.  This matches the opts.cc entry.
- Commit message: it no longer says that targets without
  TARGET_ASM_JUMP_TABLE_BASE have unchanged code.  It says that the
  option applies to every target that does not opt out.  The subject now
  ends with [PR middle-end/126236].

